WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.080 --> 00:00:09.760
On June 24, Turks go to the polls to elect
a president and parliament.

00:00:09.760 --> 00:00:14.020
Six presidential candidates are running, including
incumbent, Recep Tayyip Erdogan.

00:00:14.020 --> 00:00:17.660
Challengers have voiced radically different
visions and some polls say elections are too

00:00:17.670 --> 00:00:18.730
close to call.

00:00:18.730 --> 00:00:23.210
Erdogan should be in trouble: Turkey’s currency
is in free fall and Turkish military operations

00:00:23.210 --> 00:00:25.200
in both Syria and Iraq have floundered.

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:26.500
But does this matter?

00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:28.900
The days of free and fair elections in Turkey
are over.

00:00:28.910 --> 00:00:31.230
Erdogan rules as a dictator under a state
of emergency.

00:00:31.230 --> 00:00:35.300
He has imprisoned charismatic Kurdish candidate
Selahettin Demirtas.

00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:38.100
Mayors loyal to Erdogan block opposition campaigning.

00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:41.040
Erdogan formed his own militia to beat up
challengers,

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:45.200
and a viral video shows Erdogan telling supporters
to prevent opposition from voting.

00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:48.660
Turkish politicians say the margin of fraud
and cheating is at least 5 percent, so any

00:00:48.660 --> 00:00:53.060
challenger needs to win at least 55 percent
and even that’s no guarantee Erdogan would

00:00:53.070 --> 00:00:54.330
step down.

00:00:54.330 --> 00:00:57.760
There are open questions: Will elections go
to a second round?

00:00:57.760 --> 00:00:59.860
How many parties will enter parliament?

00:00:59.860 --> 00:01:03.000
But to consider Turkey a democracy is to believe
in unicorns.

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:07.100
There is now only one certainty: Erdogan will
rule Turkey until he dies.

00:01:08.020 --> 00:01:11.040
What do you think about Turkey's election and Turkey's future?

00:01:11.040 --> 00:01:12.520
Let us know in your comments.

00:01:12.530 --> 00:01:17.090
Also, let us know what other topics you’d
like our scholars to cover in 60 seconds,

00:01:17.090 --> 00:01:21.290
and be sure to like and subscribe for more
research and videos from AEI.

